[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2502561840","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99738#issuecomment-2502561840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99738","id":2502561840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VKhAw","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T02:42:05Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T02:42:05Z","body":"Okay, I just saw that this was changed 3 weeks ago in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/85167 \r\n\r\nThe reason why I changed it back is that in profiling the cpu usage of the spinlock was immediately apparent, so I changed it as a low-hanging fruit. \r\n\r\n@RandomShaper I think we need to revisit this, the synthetics might have looked good, but in an actual game (dome keeper in this case) this is noticeably worse than 4.2.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2502561840/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503572628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99738#issuecomment-2503572628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99738","id":2503572628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VOXyU","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T11:00:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T11:03:52Z","body":"Can you tell me more about how this affects the performance of the game, between 4.4 _master_ and 4.4 with this PR? I mean, in terms of fps, or something similar.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes two things:\r\n1. Replaces `atomic<bool>` with `atomic_flag`. On Intel, that boils down to `lock cmpxch` vs. `xchg` (note the `lock` is implicit here). According to some quotes from Intel info, none is more performant than the other. Moreover, that's the only atomic operation in practice, so both implementations have only one.\r\n2. Removes the contention optimization loop. May it be the case that the ways the spinlock is being used in the engine by itself or due to how the game uses it are leading to tons of contention, and so the issue is more about a mutex being a better choice there? Pthread's spinlock also has this sort of relaxed contention dampening loop.\r\n\r\nBonus thoughts:\r\na. With C++20 we could use `wait/notify` on the sync variable (see the spinlock example here: https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag). That would make, as far as I understand this, our spinlock much better, by not having to actually spin much. I've wondered sometimes if we should try to fool the compiler so it gives us access to that even if we're compiling with C++17. I guess all standard libraries in the compilers we care about have those implemented.\r\nb. Related to what I state in 2), I believe we should screen the whole usage of mutexes, spinlocks and their actual semantics across platforms, across the whole codebase to be sure we optimize for most cases. Otherwise, we can be going back and forth with implementations that optimize some cases while pessimizing others.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503572628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503578102","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99738#issuecomment-2503578102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99738","id":2503578102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VOZH2","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T11:02:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T11:02:45Z","body":"For convenient research, I've put together a couple of Compiler Explorer workspaces:\r\n- Prior to this PR: https://godbolt.org/z/cMG7K6PGG\r\n- With this PR: https://godbolt.org/z/8Px51M9fz","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503578102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503660578","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99738#issuecomment-2503660578","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99738","id":2503660578,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VOtQi","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T11:42:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T11:42:40Z","body":"@RandomShaper so I want to start by explaining that I made this PR not because I noticed that the spinlock implementation had changed, but rather that I was profiling master, noticed the spinlock in the profiling trace, changed it, and watched it disappear in the trace again. If the contention loop had helped then removing it should have *increased* its presence in the profiling trace. If you don't agree with that then I must be having some brain logic issue happening, which is very possible :D \r\n\r\n*specifically* in this case the problem was during culling.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2503660578/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515013251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99738#issuecomment-2515013251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99738","id":2515013251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V6A6D","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T16:20:50Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T16:20:50Z","body":"I think that makes sense. Unless there's some gotcha in how the profiler works, your logic seems solid. However, I still think we need a broader evaluation.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515013251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]